%% Lab 14: the LlamaIndex path from files to an agent's answer. Files become Documents, a splitter makes Nodes, the
%% index embeds and stores them, a retriever returns the nearest Nodes. Two ways to give that search to an agent:
%% a query engine (a second model writes a sentence from the Nodes, the step that hides the files, lit) or a
%% retriever tool (the Nodes' text and file names go to the agent). Ink: a model writes text.
%% Export: npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i lab14_documents_to_answer.mmd -o lab14_documents_to_answer.png -b white -s 2
flowchart LR
    files[36 files<br/>data/corpus] --> docs[Documents<br/>text + metadata]
    docs --> nodes[Nodes<br/>SentenceSplitter]
    nodes --> index[VectorStoreIndex<br/>one vector per Node]
    index --> ret[retriever<br/>top k Nodes<br/>with scores]
    ret --> qe[query engine<br/>a model writes<br/>a sentence]
    qe --> qet[QueryEngineTool<br/>returns the sentence]
    ret --> rt[RetrieverTool<br/>returns text<br/>and file names]
    qet --> agent[FunctionAgent<br/>model writes queries<br/>and the answer]
    rt --> agent
    classDef model fill:#0B1220,color:#FFFFFF,stroke:#0B1220
    classDef look fill:#C9F24D,color:#0B1220,stroke:#0B1220
    class agent model
    class qe look
